From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: Network commands on 127.0.0.1 by default; a load does not ask the state's size

Patches 0023 and 0024 of v1.22.2 for master. Master can bind network
commands to an address (network_cmd_bind_address), empty by default, which
is every interface; it is 127.0.0.1 here, so Quick Mode's local QUIT works
and nothing reaches the port from the network. Loading a state no longer
makes the core serialize one first to learn its size (Azahar: 1.4 s).
Patches 0021 and 0022 are in master already.

diff --git a/command.c b/command.c
index 24c627d..d9a4800 100644
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -7367,12 +7367,17 @@ bool command_event_main_state(unsigned cmd)
 
    if (savestates_enabled)
    {
-      size_t info_size;
       runloop_get_current_savestate_path(state_path,
             sizeof(state_path));
 
-      info_size          = core_serialize_size();
-      savestates_enabled = (info_size > 0);
+      /* dArkOS: only saves ask the core for the state's size first. For a
+       * load the answer was thrown away, and a core whose size is that of
+       * a fresh state (Azahar: 292 MB serialized and compressed, 1.4 s on
+       * an RG52 Mini) made one for nothing; a core that cannot load says so
+       * from retro_unserialize. */
+      if (     cmd != CMD_EVENT_LOAD_STATE
+            && cmd != CMD_EVENT_LOAD_STATE_FROM_RAM)
+         savestates_enabled = (core_serialize_size() > 0);
    }
 
   /* TODO: Load state should act in one of three ways:
diff --git a/configuration.c b/configuration.c
index 08dc2fd..220251e 100644
--- a/configuration.c
+++ b/configuration.c
@@ -6192,8 +6192,12 @@ void config_set_defaults(settings_t *target)
       configuration_set_string(settings,
             settings->arrays.netplay_mitm_server,
             def_mitm);
-   /* Empty: bind on every interface, as before the setting existed. */
-   *settings->arrays.network_cmd_bind_address = '\0';
+   /* dArkOS: 127.0.0.1, not every interface. Quick Mode closes RetroArch
+    * with `retroarch --command QUIT`, a local sender; from the network
+    * nobody should send LOAD_CORE or WRITE_CORE_RAM to a process of ark,
+    * who has sudo. Empty in the config: every interface again. */
+   strlcpy(settings->arrays.network_cmd_bind_address, "127.0.0.1",
+         sizeof(settings->arrays.network_cmd_bind_address));
    strlcpy(settings->arrays.mcp_server_bind_address, "127.0.0.1",
          sizeof(settings->arrays.mcp_server_bind_address));
    *settings->arrays.mcp_server_token = '\0';
